From 518d2dc3a82d9ca7b9114b171aaa0c3a2e00d0c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Gunthorpe <jgg@nvidia.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 15:24:07 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] drtm: validate two-stage DCE measurement

Test 116 treated EVTYPE_ARM_DCE like an ordinary firmware measurement and
compared its selected-bank digest directly with
Hash_selected(0x00). DEN0113 1.4B section 4.8.2 defines the DCE
measurement as a two-stage hash: the D-CRTM first computes DCE_digest with
the selected hashing algorithm advertised in DRTM_FEATURES, then sends
DCE_digest to the TPM's HASH_DATA interface, which hashes it again before
extending it into PCR[17] "for all enabled PCR banks." Comparing against
Hash_selected(0x00) skips that second hashing stage and ignores all other
active PCR banks. The test also did not validate the event's dense TPMT_HA
payload, accepted incomplete digest lists, and allowed duplicate DCE and
DCE_PUBKEY records.

Represent the fixed non-distinct-DCE measurement with known-answer vectors
for SHA-256, SHA-384, and SHA-512 firmware selection and
SHA-1/SHA-256/SHA-384/SHA-512 active banks. Per section 4.8.2
("digests: TPML_DIGEST_VALUES struct which contains the values of
Hash(DCE_digest) for all enabled PCR banks"), require EVTYPE_ARM_DCE
to contain every advertised bank's Hash_bank(DCE_digest), and
validate its exact packed algorithm-plus-DCE_digest payload.

Keep EVTYPE_ARM_DCE_PUBKEY as an ordinary selected-bank measurement of the
empty public key, requiring exactly one Hash_selected(0x00) digest and
empty event data, matching the EVTYPE_ARM_DCE_PUBKEY definition in DEN0113
1.4B section 3.17.2 (Table 19). Reject duplicate records while retaining
the required PCR placement and missing-event checks. Static vectors keep
the test usable in non-UEFI builds without adding a target-specific crypto
library dependency.

Signed-off-by: Jason Gunthorpe <jgg@nvidia.com>
